              "@type": "uco-observable:ExtractedString",
              "uco-observable:stringValue": "Query Reports Utilities Help Log Out\n\nJFA\n\nU.S. District Court\nDistrict of Wyoming (Casper)\nCRIMINAL DOCKET FOR CASE #: 1:22-cr-00137-ABJ All Defendants\n\nCase title: USA v. Smith Date Filed: 11/17/2022\n\nDate Terminated: 07/31/2023\n\nAssigned to: Honorable Alan B Johnson\n\nDefendant (1)\nKyle Bradley Smith represented by David Weiss\nTERMINATED: 07/31/2023 Federal Public Defender\nDistrict of Wyoming\n5353 Yellowstone Road\nRoom 207\nCheyenne, WY 82009\n307-772-2781\nEmail: David_Weiss@fd.org\nLEAD ATTORNEY\nATTORNEY TO BE NOTICED\nDesignation: Federal Public Defender\n\nPending Counts Disposition\n420 months, concurrent with Count 4 and with Sheridan County\n18 U.S.C. \u00a7 2251(a), (e) Sexual Exploitation of Children District Court Docket CR-2016-18; 15 years supervised release,\n(2) concurrent with Count 4; $100 special assessment per count;\n$206.67 restitution\n420 months, concurrent with Count 2 and with Sheridan County\n18 U.S.C. \u00a7 2251(a), (e) Attempted Sexual Exploitation of\nDistrict Court Docket CR-2016-18; 15 years supervised release,\nChildren\nconcurrent with Count 2; $100 special assessment per count;\n(4)\n$1,440 Restitution\n\nHighest Offense Level (Opening)\nFelony\nTerminated Counts Disposition\n18 U.S.C. \u00a7\u00a7 2252A(a)(2)(A) and (b)(1) Distribution of Child Count dismissed on motion of the United States; however,\nPornography pursuant to the agreement in this matter, defendant agreed to\n(1) pay $3,000 restitution to the victim of this count\n18 U.S.C. \u00a7 2422(b) Attempting to Entice Minor to Engage in\nIllegal Sexual Activity Dismissed on motion of the United States\n(3)\n18 U.S.C. \u00a7 2251(a), (e) Attempted Sexual Exploitation of\nChildren Dismissed on motion of the United States\n(5)\n18 U.S.C. \u00a7 2260A Commission of a Felony Sex Offense by an\nIndividual Required to Register as a Sex Offender Dismissed on motion of the United States\n(6)\n\nHighest Offense Level (Terminated)\nFelony\n\nComplaints Disposition\nNone\n\nPlaintiff\nUSA represented by Zachary Seth Griswold\nUNITED STATES ATTORNEYS OFFICE\n2120 Capitol Avenue\n4th Floor\nPO Box 668\nCheyenne, WY 82001\n307-772-2124\nFax: 307-772-2123\nEmail: Seth.griswold@usdoj.gov\nLEAD ATTORNEY\nATTORNEY TO BE NOTICED\nDesignation: United States Attorney\n\nDate Filed # Docket Text\n11/17/2022 1 INDICTMENT as to Kyle Bradley Smith (1) count(s) 1, 2, 3, 4-5, 6 (Court Staff, sbh) (Additional attachment(s) added on 11/18/2022: # 1\nSealed Indictment) (Court Staff, sbh). (Entered: 11/18/2022)\n11/17/2022 2 Praecipe for Warrant by Plaintiff USA as to Defendant(s) Kyle Bradley Smith (Court Staff, sbh) (Entered: 11/18/2022)\n11/17/2022 3 Warrant Issued as to Kyle Bradley Smith (Court Staff, sbh) (Entered: 11/18/2022)\n11/17/2022 4 MOTION for Detention Hearing by USA as to Defendant(s) Kyle Bradley Smith (Court Staff, sbh) (Entered: 11/18/2022)\n02/27/2023 5 NON-PUBLIC DOCUMENT pursuant to the Judicial Conference Policy on Privacy and Public Access - MOTION for Writ of Habeas\nCorpus ad prosequendum by USA as to Defendant(s) Kyle Bradley Smith. (Attachments: # 1 Proposed Order, # 2 Writ)(Griswold, Zachary)\n(Entered: 02/27/2023)\n02/28/2023 6 NON-PUBLIC DOCUMENT pursuant to the Judicial Conference Policy on Privacy and Public Access - ORDER granting 5 Motion for\nWrit of Habeas Corpus ad prosequendum as to Kyle Bradley Smith (1) by the Honorable Alan B. Johnson (Court Staff, sbh) (Entered:\n02/28/2023)\n02/28/2023 7 NON-PUBLIC DOCUMENT pursuant to the Judicial Conference Policy on Privacy and Public Access - Writ of Habeas Corpus ad\nProsequendum Issued as to Kyle Bradley Smith (Emailed to USMS on this date) (Court Staff, sbh) (Entered: 02/28/2023)\n03/03/2023 8 (TEXT-ONLY) NOTICE OF HEARING as to Kyle Bradley Smith, Jury trial vacated, VIA ZOOM -\n\nNOTE:\n\n1. This proceeding will be held via Zoom Video/Web Conferencing with all participants appearing remotely; the Zoom ID and Passcode\nwill be provided separately to the participants email address of record.\n\n2. Participants should connect to the proceeding 15 minutes prior to its scheduled start time to allow for troubleshooting of any connectivity\nissues.\n\n3. To ensure the record is of the best quality, participants are encouraged to utilize a headset to reduce static and background noise. If not\nusing a headset, participants must ensure the audio feed at their location is muted when not speaking.\n\n***REMINDER: Recording or broadcasting of this hearing is prohibited. ***\n\nInitial Appearance set for 3/6/2023 at 10:00 AM before Honorable Kelly H Rankin. (Court Staff, smxb) (Entered: 03/03/2023)\n03/06/2023 9 NOTICE OF ATTORNEY APPEARANCE: David Weiss appearing for defendant Kyle Bradley Smith (Weiss, David) (Entered:\n03/06/2023)\n03/06/2023 10 Minute Entry: Initial Appearance as to Kyle Bradley Smith held on 3/6/2023. Defendant detained. ***Location start as to Kyle Bradley\nSmith, ***Procedural Interval start as to Kyle Bradley Smith Proceedings held before Honorable Kelly H Rankin. (Court Reporter FTR.)\n(Court Staff, smxb) (Entered: 03/06/2023)\n03/06/2023 11 WRITTEN CONSENT TO APPEAR BY VIDEO CONFERENCE by defendant Kyle Bradley Smith (Court Staff, smxb) (Entered:\n03/06/2023)\n03/06/2023 12 NON-PUBLIC DOCUMENT pursuant to the Judicial Conference Policy on Privacy and Public Access - CJA 23 Financial Affidavit by\nKyle Bradley Smith (Court Staff, smxb) (Entered: 03/06/2023)\n03/06/2023 13 ORDER OF TEMPORARY DETENTION PENDING HEARING PURSUANT TO BAIL REFORM ACT as to Kyle Bradley Smith by the\nHonorable Kelly H Rankin.(Court Staff, smxb) (Entered: 03/06/2023)\n03/06/2023 14 (TEXT-ONLY) NOTICE OF HEARING as to Kyle Bradley Smith, VIA ZOOM -\n\nNOTE:\n\n1. This proceeding will be held via Zoom Video/Web Conferencing with all participants appearing remotely; the Zoom ID and Passcode\nwill be provided separately to the participants email address of record.\n\n2. Participants should connect to the proceeding 15 minutes prior to its scheduled start time to allow for troubleshooting of any connectivity\nissues.\n\n3. To ensure the record is of the best quality, participants are encouraged to utilize a headset to reduce static and background noise. If not\nusing a headset, participants must ensure the audio feed at their location is muted when not speaking.\n\n***REMINDER: Recording or broadcasting of this hearing is prohibited. ***\n\nArraignment/Detention set for 3/9/2023 at 11:00 AM before Honorable Kelly H Rankin.(Court Staff, smxb) (Entered: 03/06/2023)\n03/06/2023 15 Warrant Returned Executed on 3/3/2023 in case as to Kyle Bradley Smith. (Court Staff, stmo) (Entered: 03/06/2023)\n03/09/2023 16 SEALED DOCUMENT - PRETRIAL SERVICES BOND MEMO as to Kyle Bradley Smith. Access granted to: Zachary Seth Griswold,\nDavid Weiss. (sbila, ) (Entered: 03/09/2023)\n03/09/2023 17 Minute Entry: Arraignment as to Kyle Bradley Smith (1) Count 1,2,3,4-5,6 held on 3/9/2023. Defendant pled not guilty. Speedy trial is\ncalculated as 5/12/23. Minute Entry: Detention Hearing as to Kyle Bradley Smith held on 3/9/2023. Defendant detained. Proceedings held\nbefore Honorable Kelly H Rankin. (Court Reporter Jan Davis.) (Court Staff, smxb) (Entered: 03/09/2023)\n03/09/2023 18 WRITTEN CONSENT TO APPEAR BY VIDEO CONFERENCE by defendant Kyle Bradley Smith (Court Staff, smxb) (Entered:\n03/09/2023)\n03/09/2023 19 ORDER for Discovery and Scheduling Order as to Kyle Bradley Smith. Plea Agreement shall be filed with the Court no later than seven (7)\ndays prior to trial by the Honorable Kelly H Rankin.(Court Staff, smxb) (Entered: 03/09/2023)\n03/09/2023 20 ORDER for Grand Jury Transcripts as to Kyle Bradley Smith by the Honorable Kelly H Rankin.(Court Staff, smxb) (Entered: 03/09/2023)\n03/09/2023 21 ORDER OF DETENTION as to Kyle Bradley Smith by the Honorable Kelly H Rankin.(Court Staff, smxb) (Main Document 21 replaced to\ninclude Judge's signature and file stamp on 3/10/2023) (Court Staff, smxb). (Entered: 03/09/2023)\n03/09/2023 22 (TEXT-ONLY) NOTICE OF HEARING as to Kyle Bradley Smith, IN-PERSON Jury Trial set for 5/8/2023 01:30 PM in Cheyenne\nCourtroom No. 2 (Room No. 2116) before Honorable Alan B Johnson. (Court Staff, smxb) (Entered: 03/09/2023)\n03/27/2023 23 NOTICE OF INTENT TO OFFER EXPERT TESTIMONY by USA as to defendant Kyle Bradley Smith. (Attachments: # 1 Exhibit\nCurriculum Vitae for SA Carpenter, # 2 Exhibit Curriculum Vitae for CFA Forness)(Griswold, Zachary) (Entered: 03/27/2023)\n04/21/2023 24 EX PARTE/NON-PUBLIC DOCUMENT pursuant to the Judicial Conference Policy on Privacy and Public Access - PLEA AGREEMENT\nas to Kyle Bradley Smith. (Court Staff, stmo). Modified on 4/21/2023 (Court Staff, stmo). (Entered: 04/21/2023)\n04/24/2023 25 (TEXT-ONLY) NOTICE OF HEARING as to Kyle Bradley Smith. Change of Plea Hearing set for 4/27/2023 at 3:00 PM IN PERSON\nin Cheyenne Courtroom No. 2 (Room No. 2116) before Honorable Alan B Johnson. (Court Staff, ssw) (Entered: 04/24/2023)\n04/26/2023 26 EX-PARTE/NON-PUBLIC DOCUMENT pursuant to the Judicial Conference Policy on Privacy and Public Access - PROSECUTOR'S\nSTATEMENT filed by USA as to Plaintiff USA, Defendant Kyle Bradley Smith (Griswold, Zachary) (Entered: 04/26/2023)\n04/27/2023 27 Minute Entry: Change of Plea Hearing as to Kyle Bradley Smith held on 4/27/2023. Guilty plea entered to Counts 2 and 4. Defendant\nremanded. Proceedings held before Honorable Alan B. Johnson. (Court Reporter: Melanie Sonntag) (Court Staff, sbh) (Entered:\n04/27/2023)\n04/27/2023 28 (TEXT-ONLY) NOTICE OF HEARING as to Kyle Bradley Smith: Sentencing set for 7/31/2023 at 1:30 PM in Cheyenne Courtroom\nNo. 2 (Room No. 2116) before Honorable Alan B. Johnson (Jury trial vacated) (Court Staff, sbh) (Entered: 04/27/2023)\n06/08/2023 29 SEALED DOCUMENT - PRESENTENCE REPORT as to Kyle Bradley Smith. Access granted to: Zachary Seth Griswold, David Weiss.\nLast day to file response to PSR is 6/25/2023. (svenegas) (Entered: 06/08/2023)\n06/08/2023 30 SEALED DOCUMENT - PRESENTENCE REPORT RECOMMENDATIONS as to Kyle Bradley Smith. Access granted to: No Outside\nUsers. (svenegas) (Entered: 06/08/2023)\n06/22/2023 31 EX-PARTE DOCUMENT - OBJECTIONS/RESPONSES TO PRESENTENCE INVESTIGATION REPORT as to defendant Kyle Bradley\nSmith. NO OBJECTIONS SUBMITTED. (Weiss, David) (Entered: 06/22/2023)\n06/26/2023 32 EX-PARTE DOCUMENT - OBJECTIONS/RESPONSES TO PRESENTENCE INVESTIGATION REPORT as to defendant Kyle Bradley\nSmith. NO OBJECTIONS SUBMITTED. (Griswold, Zachary) (Entered: 06/26/2023)\n07/06/2023 33 SEALED DOCUMENT - ADDENDUM TO PRESENTENCE REPORT as to Kyle Bradley Smith. Access granted to: Zachary Seth\nGriswold, David Weiss. (svenegas) (Entered: 07/06/2023)\n07/06/2023 34 SEALED DOCUMENT - REVISED PRESENTENCE REPORT as to Kyle Bradley Smith. Access granted to: Zachary Seth Griswold,\nDavid Weiss. (svenegas) (Entered: 07/06/2023)\n07/06/2023 35 SEALED DOCUMENT - REVISED PRESENTENCE REPORT RECOMMENDATIONS as to Kyle Bradley Smith. Access granted to: No\nOutside Users. (svenegas) (Entered: 07/06/2023)\n07/31/2023 36 Minute Entry: Sentencing held on 7/31/2023 for Kyle Bradley Smith (1). Count(s) 1, Count dismissed on motion of the United States;\nhowever, pursuant to the agreement in this matter, defendant agreed to pay $3,000 restitution to the victim of this count; Count(s) 2, 420\nmonths, concurrent with Count 4 and with Sheridan County District Court Docket CR-2016-18; 15 years supervised release, concurrent\nwith Count 4; $100 special assessment per count; $206.67 restitution; Count(s) 3, 5, 6, Dismissed on motion of the United States; Count(s)\n4, 420 months, concurrent with Count 2 and with Sheridan County District Court Docket CR-2016-18; 15 years supervised release,\nconcurrent with Count 2; $100 special assessment per count; Restitution to remain open for up to 90 days. Defendant remanded.\nProceedings held before Honorable Alan B. Johnson. (Court Reporter: Melanie Sonntag) (Court Staff, sbh) (Entered: 07/31/2023)\n07/31/2023 37 JUDGMENT and COMMITMENT as to Kyle Bradley Smith (1) by the Honorable Alan B. Johnson. Count(s) 1, Count dismissed on\nmotion of the United States; however, pursuant to the agreement in this matter, defendant agreed to pay $3,000 restitution to the victim of\nthis count; Count(s) 2, 420 months, concurrent with Count 4 and with Sheridan County District Court Docket CR-2016-18; 15 years\nsupervised release, concurrent with Count 4; $100 special assessment per count; $206.67 restitution; Count(s) 3, 5, 6, Dismissed on motion\nof the United States; Count(s) 4, 420 months, concurrent with Count 2 and with Sheridan County District Court Docket CR-2016-18; 15\nyears supervised release, concurrent with Count 2; $100 special assessment per count; Restitution to remain open for up to 90 days. (Court\nStaff, sbh) (Entered: 07/31/2023)\n10/30/2023 38 NON-PUBLIC DOCUMENT pursuant to the Judicial Conference Policy on Privacy and Public Access - MOTION for Order Restitution by\nUSA as to Defendant(s) Kyle Bradley Smith. (Attachments: # 1 Proposed Order)(Griswold, Zachary) (Entered: 10/30/2023)\n11/02/2023 39 NON-PUBLIC DOCUMENT pursuant to the Judicial Conference Policy on Privacy and Public Access - RESTITUTION ORDER re 38\nMotion for Order as to Kyle Bradley Smith (1) by the Honorable Alan B. Johnson (Court Staff, sbh) (Entered: 11/02/2023)\n\nPACER Service Center\nTransaction Receipt\n06/28/2026 19:28:39\nPACER\nmrinaal_ramachandran Client Code:\nLogin:\nSearch 1:22-cr-00137-\nDescription: Docket Report\nCriteria: ABJ\nBillable\n6 Cost: 0.60\nPages:"
